/-!
# Witness table for Rudvalis seed-set coverage

The finite index set has 424125 rows; this alone makes no claim about an orbit.
Each 397-bit row contains 28 twelve-bit point labels, then three nineteen-bit
indices (a-successor, b-successor, forest parent), then a four-bit edge label.
The b-successor uses the inverse of the original GAP b permutation, as required
for the model's left action. A forest edge maps its child to its parent under
the model's candidate generator. Roots occupy indices 0--75 in sector order.

Blocks contain 256 rows and are selected by balanced comparison trees.
All discovery outputs are untrusted until checked by the separate proofs.
See `source/Generate.py`; the original data are regenerated by
`Representatives/source/Generate.py`. Source application: Aschbacher--Smith,
printed p.511 (PDF p.528), citing Aschbacher (1986), no.343.
-/

